From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 07:20:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: give Orange Pi 5B a default DP lane map

The combo PHY can be powered by the built-in XHCI driver before the Type-C
orientation and mode switches have reported their state.  Without a default
DP lane map that first power-on configures the analog block for USB only.
Later selecting pin assignment D updates the software lane map, but does not
necessarily rebuild the already running analog block, leaving AUX requests to
time out despite asserted HPD.

Use the normal-orientation two-lane mapping used by the upstream IndieDroid
Nova USB-C DP description.  The Type-C orientation switch still replaces this
mapping when a cable is inserted in the reverse orientation.

This is an experimental Orange Pi 5B enablement workaround.  Drop it once the
upstream board DTS provides a working USB-C DP topology and initial lane map.

Signed-off-by: Codex <codex@openai.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-orangepi-5.dtsi | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-orangepi-5.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-orangepi-5.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-orangepi-5.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-orangepi-5.dtsi
@@ -865,6 +865,7 @@
 
 &usbdp_phy0 {
 	mode-switch;
+	rockchip,dp-lane-mux = <2 3>;
 	orientation-switch;
 	sbu1-dc-gpios = <&gpio4 RK_PA5 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
 	sbu2-dc-gpios = <&gpio4 RK_PA7 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
-- 
